speechtext:
I would like to suggest that in the Parliament buildings which are being erected, some memorial or tablet be placed to commemorate the death of our late colleague, Mr. Law, who lost his life there under very distressing circumstances. No tablet and no stone of any kind marks his resting place, and it would be a nice idea and a thoughtful act on our part if somewhere in the corridors of the new Parliament buildings it were to be memorialized that
[Mr. Graham.}
the remains of the late Mr. Law rest in that building.
